  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation sits on `fn[node_content]` in `impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Graph]`, an explicit function with a body, inside fenced commentary. That is a permitted form.\n\nThe reason is substantive and matches the current source:\n- The enclosing test, `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`, uses a script that calls only `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`.\n- It asserts that the only recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(1, (), edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2]))`. It also asserts the edge lookup count, so the selection is not re-listed.\n- `edge_fingerprint` and `prepare_edges` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` build the fingerprint from `node_path` and `outgoing_edges`. They never call `node_content`.\n- So the callback is required by the `Graph` trait but is not reached on this path. If it were reached, it would be an unwanted content read, and the `panic!` body makes that fail the test.\n\nThe function is a deliberate guard rather than code that is merely hard to cover. The item has no {impl} or {test} reference of its own, so the citation is not redundant. The citation is accepted.",
